# Technical review rules

This English reference follows sections 1, 4, and 5 of the technical self-check design at baseline 0.2. The [Chinese export](TC规则.md) and its [provenance](TC规则.provenance.json) retain the original wording, source and export hashes, section selection, and identities of the unbundled source index and scoring proposal. Apply the [shared conventions](共同约定.md), current task, and effective decisions to determine scope.

## 1. Purpose of technical self-check

Check whether a reader can identify the intended work, responsible modules, data handling, recovery actions, completion criteria, and prerequisites. Report concrete findings and the evidence behind each conclusion. Use the technical summary for orientation and retain the details of modules, runtime scenarios, decisions, quality, and risks. [arc42 solution strategy](https://docs.arc42.org/section-4/) and [runtime view](https://docs.arc42.org/section-6/)

### 1.1 Evidence levels and supported conclusions

| Level | Review object and method | Supported conclusion | Evidence boundary |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| L1 Structure | Check fields, IDs, references, versions, dependencies, and trace links. Use repeatable rules and inspect false positives. | Whether a stated structural condition is satisfied. | Design soundness, core feasibility, and actual behavior require their own evidence. |
| L2 Semantics | Trace requirement meanings, module responsibilities, both sides of interfaces, data and states, and consistency between tasks and acceptance. Verify sources and obtain independent review where needed. | A supported design judgment or concrete conflict within the stated scope. | Model accuracy, trial completion, and user approval require their own evidence. |
| L3 Feasibility verification | Verify the platform, version, and environment needed to establish a core hypothesis. Read official material and examine actual prototypes, operations, files, or logs where required. | Evidence for the exact hypothesis. Record the observed trial as passed, failed, or unverified. | Limit findings to the actual hypothesis, version, platform, and environment. |

Specify the necessary levels for each rule. Official documentation can establish its stated version facts. Use actual project evidence for implementation behavior and execute trials where the original rule requires them. Keep design review status **satisfied / unsatisfied / unchecked / inapplicable with reason** separate from actual trial status **passed / failed / unverified / inapplicable with reason**.

### 1.2 Source methods and project rules

Use arc42 for document structure and representative scenarios, NASA for design review, traceability, and prototype verification, MADR for recording decisions, and Google SRE for actionable readiness checks that can be scaled to scope. The technical review IDs, severity, state transitions, and stop conditions are project design proposals. Obtain actual user approval and budget independently. The original source index records source versions and the scope of adoption. [Google SRE launch readiness](https://sre.google/sre-book/reliable-product-launches/)

Determine cancellation, retry, upgrade, and failure coverage from confirmed goals, actual capabilities, and risk. Give reasons for exclusions and retain critical risks in the review.

